The studies HLV-204-201, RSP-118-302 and DRM-501-201, their sponsors, products, sites,
participants and verbatim terms are fictional. The Study Medical Dictionary (SMD) and the Study
Drug Dictionary (SDD) are training dictionaries shaped like MedDRA and WHODrug Global: their
names, codes, hierarchy, trade names and class codes are invented, and they contain no MedDRA
or WHODrug content. Ingredient names are public International Nonproprietary Names. MedDRA is
a trademark of ICH, maintained by the MSSO; WHODrug is a product of the Uppsala Monitoring
Centre; both are named for education only and real use requires their licences. The coding
conventions are written in this app's own words on the principles of the ICH "MedDRA Term
Selection: Points to Consider". The Standard Search Groups are invented and contain no SMQ content. The language versions are
training translations of a few terms. The AI coding assistant is a simulation with invented
figures, not a real model.
Not a validated system; the signatures are practice
signatures; no real study data. Everything stays in the browser.

The dictionaries are shared with the CDM Query & Edit-Check Console by the same author
(Apache License 2.0).

